-- a scope respects identity of molecules: identical molecules are in it or out of it together. No
-- scope can distinguish molecules that are identical, however it is written — which is what makes
-- the carrier of identity the thing that decides what a claim covers.
scope-respects : (S : Scope) → (M : Mol) → (N : Mol) → M ≡ N → S M → S N
scope-respects S M N p s = transport (λ i → S (p i)) s
